    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d282">

                <pb facs="0334" n="1068" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1068"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Breckinridge to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-08-28"><hi rendition="#italic">August 28, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received Sept. 19.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 133.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 116, of July 24, in
                    regard to the refusal of the Russian consul at New York to visé the passports of
                    American citizens of Jewish descent, I now have to inclose copy and translation
                    of a note dated August 12/24, from Prince Lobanow, in response to my request for
                    a copy of the laws and regulations bearing upon the administration of foreign
                    Jews.</p>
                <p>I also inclose copy and translation of the laws in question.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clifton R. Breckinridge.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d282-a1.xml" xpointer="d282-a1"/>
